## ADT Cuaderno 3 HTML Style Guide

Reference pages: 9_0_adt.html, 9_1_adt.html, 13_0_adt.html, 16_0_adt.html, 19_0_adt.html, 20_0_adt.html, 21_1_adt.html, 25_0_adt.html

### Layout Shell
- The application wraps your HTML in the `<body>` shell and injects the persistent `interface-container` and `nav-container` elements for you.
- Start your markup with the page wrapper: `flex justify-center items-start min-h-[calc(100dvh-100px)]`
- Nest the content container inside: `container mx-auto max-w-5xl bg-white rounded-lg lg:px-24 md:px-12 sm:px-6 pt-12 pb-12` with `id="content"`

```html
<div class="flex justify-center items-start min-h-[calc(100dvh-100px)]">
  <div class="container mx-auto max-w-5xl bg-white rounded-lg lg:px-24 md:px-12 sm:px-6 pt-12 pb-12" id="content">
    <!-- section content -->
  </div>
</div>
```

### Headings & Intro Text
- Primary heading (H1): `text-5xl font-bold mb-4 text-amber-700`
- Secondary heading (H2 if needed): `text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-amber-500`
- Instruction line: `text-xl mb-8` and prepend `<i class="fas fa-pen-to-square text-blue-700 mr-2"></i>` or `<i class="fas fa-book text-blue-700 mr-2"></i>`

### Regular Text (Narrative & Section Content)
- **NO background color** - Regular narrative paragraphs and section text should have NO highlight/background
- Use plain `<p class="mb-4">` with `<span data-id="...">` children for text blocks
- Text color is default (black/gray-900) - readable on white background

### Highlighted Text Blocks & Callouts
**ONLY use background colors for special callout boxes, NOT regular section text:**
- Info card (e.g., "Recuerda que..."): `bg-amber-50 p-4 rounded-lg text-amber-900 shadow-sm`
- Instruction boxes: `bg-amber-50 p-4 rounded-lg`
- Special highlight tiles (grids): `bg-amber-50 p-3 rounded-md text-center font-medium`

### Forms & Inputs
- Inline label/input row: `flex gap-2 items-center` with input `grow p-2 border border-gray-300 rounded`
- Stacked grid: `grid grid-cols-1 gap-6` and labels `font-semibold whitespace-nowrap`
- Radio cards: `flex items-center p-4 border-2 border-green-50 bg-green-50 rounded-lg cursor-pointer hover:bg-green-100 [&:has(:checked)]:bg-green-200 [&:has(:checked)]:border-green-400`

### Interactive Elements
- Draggable token: `activity-item` base with `cursor-move` and color-coded backgrounds (`bg-yellow-100`, `bg-teal-100`, `bg-green-100`)
- Dropzone: `flex gap-4 items-center border border-gray-300 p-2 pl-4 rounded-lg min-h-[62px]`
- Word chips: `bg-gray-100 p-2 px-4 rounded-full inline-block`

### **CRITICAL: Sorting Activity Structure (activity_sorting)**
When section type is `activity_sorting`, you MUST use this exact structure:

**Word Cards (draggable items):**
- Class: `word-card` (NOT `activity-item`)
- Attribute: `data-activity-item="unique-id"` - REQUIRED
- Attribute: `data-id="text-id"` - REQUIRED
- Attribute: `draggable="true"`

**Categories (drop zones):**
- Class: `category` - REQUIRED
- Attribute: `data-activity-category="category-name"` - REQUIRED
- Must contain: `<ul class="word-list"></ul>` - REQUIRED

Example sorting activity:
```html
<!-- Word bank -->
<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
  <div class="word-card bg-yellow-100 p-2 px-4 rounded-full cursor-move" 
       data-activity-item="word-1" data-id="text-1" draggable="true">Word 1</div>
</div>

<!-- Categories -->
<div class="category border p-4 rounded-lg" data-activity-category="cat-1">
  <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Category 1</h3>
  <ul class="word-list"></ul>
</div>
```

### Imagery & Media
- **Plain images (NO decorations)** - Images should be displayed cleanly without borders, padding, or shadows
- Standard image: `class="w-full max-w-sm rounded-lg"`
- **Two-column layout** - Use `flex flex-col-reverse md:flex-row gap-4 md:items-center` to show image FIRST on mobile
- Always include descriptive `alt` and `aria-label`

### Color Palette (Tailwind classes)
- Primary text accent: `text-amber-700`
- Secondary accent: `text-amber-500`
- Instruction icon: `text-blue-700`
- Highlight backgrounds: `bg-amber-50`, `bg-yellow-100`, `bg-teal-100`, `bg-green-50`, `bg-green-100`, `bg-green-200`
- Neutral surfaces: `bg-white`, `border-gray-300`, `bg-gray-100`

## Input Data
You are given:
1. **Original textbook page image** - Use for visual context and positioning reference. DO NOT add extra text from the image.
2. **Extracted text** - Use ONLY this text. You may slightly modify for flow but must preserve all provided text IDs.
3. **Images** - Only use provided images with their exact IDs. No placeholder images.
4. **Section type** - Determines the appropriate layout pattern.

## CRITICAL REQUIREMENTS

### Structure
1. **Layout Shell** - The system already provides the `<body>` wrapper plus the interface/navigation containers. Your response MUST begin with the page wrapper `<div class="flex justify-center items-start min-h-[calc(100dvh-100px)]">` and include the nested content container `<div id="content" ...>`. Do **NOT** output `<body>`, `<div id="interface-container">`, or `<div id="nav-container">`.

2. **Single Section** - There MUST be exactly ONE `<section>` tag in the HTML.

3. **Section Attributes**:
   - `role="article"` for narrative/informational content
   - `role="activity"` for interactive/exercise content
   - `data-section-type` attribute with the provided section type (e.g., `data-section-type="text-and-images"`)

### Text & Data IDs
4. **All text elements** MUST have a `data-id` attribute matching the provided text ID.

5. **Text must be direct children** - Elements with `data-id` MUST contain plain text as immediate children:
   - ✅ CORRECT: `<p data-id="text-1-0">This is text</p>`
   - ✅ CORRECT: `<strong><p data-id="text-1-0">This is text</p></strong>`
   - ❌ WRONG: `<p data-id="text-1-0"><strong>This is text</strong></p>`

6. **Use provided IDs only** - DO NOT create additional data-ids beyond those provided.

### Images
7. **Only provided images** - DO NOT add placeholder images or any `<img>` tags without a corresponding image ID.

8. **All images need data-id** - Every `<img>` MUST have `data-id` matching the provided image ID:
   ```html
   <img src="./images/filename.svg" data-id="img-26-2" alt="Description" class="w-full max-w-sm rounded-lg" />
   ```

9. **Appropriate sizing** - Use style guide classes (`max-w-sm`, responsive layouts) to prevent images from dominating the page.

### Activity-Specific Requirements
10. **Sorting Activities (activity_sorting)** - When section type is `activity_sorting`, you MUST:
    - Use `word-card` class (NOT `activity-item`) for draggable items
    - Add BOTH `data-activity-item` AND `data-id` to each word card
    - Use `category` class for drop zones
    - Add `data-activity-category` attribute to each category
    - Include `<ul class="word-list"></ul>` inside each category
    - See "Sorting Activity Structure" in style guide for complete example

### Styling & Components
11. **Follow the style guide** - Reference the included style guide above for all styling patterns, components, and color choices.

### Content Rules
12. **Text modification** - You MAY slightly truncate or exclude text for pedagogical reasons, but you MUST:
    - Remove the entire element AND its data-id if excluding text
    - Never split a data-id across multiple elements
    - Preserve the meaning and flow

13. **Language** - For `textarea` and `input` placeholder text, use this language: {{ language }}

14. **Accessibility** - Include proper `aria-label`, `role`, and semantic HTML. Ensure readable contrast as specified in the style guide.

## Design Goals
- Create warm, inviting, magical pages that feel educational yet fun
- Use generous whitespace and clear visual hierarchy
- Match the textbook's aesthetic while enhancing with digital interactivity
- Prioritize clarity and accessibility for young learners

## Response Format
You must return a structured JSON response with TWO fields:
1. **reasoning**: A brief explanation of your layout and styling choices (1-2 sentences)
2. **content**: The complete HTML body content following the exact structure shown in examples

Example response structure:
```json
{
  "reasoning": "I created a narrative section with plain paragraphs for the story text and positioned the images in a responsive grid layout.",
  "content": "<div class=\"flex justify-center items-start min-h-[calc(100dvh-100px)]\">...</div>"
}
```

Take your time. Think carefully about layout, component choice, and styling. Make it beautiful!
